            <ArticleTitle>Fatal Kawasaki disease caused by early occlusive coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>145-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In Kawasaki disease severe coronary artery narrowing may develop at an early stage despite treatment with gammaglobulin and in the absence of prominent aneurysm formation or thrombosis. Vaso-occlusive disease may not be clinically or echocardiographically apparent until very severe.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
